Z||000000||fotofrank||07-19-2000||10:04 PM||||I have an '84 2.5 into wich I installed the ralley gauges. I got an oil pressuer sensor(used )from the fiero warehouse. It does read oil pressure and the original was just a switch. The problem is the battery drains in about 7-9 days if the oil sensor has it's connector conected. The schematics all show 1 wire (12 volt) to the oil switch/sensor but I have 3. anyone know what the problem might be. I suspect the sensor is bad and the 12 volts is gong to ground. I know that if I connect the oil sensor the battery shows a drain to ground.  (the ole' lightbulb between the negative lead and the battery trick)Thanks.<P>------------------<BR>Peace and Happiness<BR>Frank and his fotoflash, an '84 SE 2M4<BR>http://fotofrank.homestead.com/foto1.html||||reg||4
Z||000001||Oreif||07-20-2000||01:42 AM||||Could it be the Fuel pump switch in the oil sender? I know that the Fuel pump is wired thru the oil sensor so if you have no pressure you would have no fuel. I don't have a wiring diagram for an 84 but the 86 shows a orange/black wire (noted as pin A)as the power side and the tan/white wire (noted as pin C) as the fuel pump side and going to the ALCL connector pin G. If you have the car off and power on the tan/white wire that could be the problem. I also looked up the ralley gage and it shows a tan wire (noted as B on the sender side) is the only wire for the gage.  <P><BR>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 07-20-2000).]||||reg||1
